babashka.ffi examples
---------------------
  Copyright (c) 2026 Michiel Borkent (@borkdude)
  https://github.com/babashka/ffi
  Licensed under the MIT license, reproduced below.

  Three examples here are Clojure ports of programs from the babashka/ffi
  examples directory, not of raylib's own examples:

    helitorus  <- examples/helitorus.clj  (1034e56, 2026-08-28)
    doom       <- examples/doom.clj       (1034e56, 2026-08-28)
    pacman     <- examples/pacman.clj     (94ccd77, 2026-08-31)

  The geometry, level data, game rules and palettes came from those
  originals and are substantially unchanged. What the ports here changed is
  how the program reaches raylib: babashka.ffi calls became this project's
  wrapper, and the buffers gained jolt type hints. The shared data is the
  quickest way to check the claim, since doom's sixteen level rows and
  pacman's twenty-one maze rows are byte-identical to the originals, and
  helitorus keeps the same hsl(337..349, 100..78%, 17..72%) palette.

  The README's example table names babashka/ffi as the source for these
  three, the way it names the raylib example for every other port.

  Michiel Borkent's own header for helitorus credits it one step further
  back, to a Scittle demo drawing the same figure to a 2D canvas. That
  attribution is repeated here rather than independently verified.

